<article class="env-lemma" id="0BCV">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0BCV">Lemma <span data-tag="0BCV">31.17.5</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a separated locally Noetherian scheme. Let $U \subset X$ be an affine open. For every generic point $\xi $ of an irreducible component of $X \setminus U$ the local ring $\mathcal{O}_{X, \xi }$ has dimension $\leq 1$. If $U$ is dense or if $\xi $ is in the closure of $U$, then $\dim (\mathcal{O}_{X, \xi }) = 1$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/0BCU" data-tag="0BCU">31.17.4</a> because the morphism $U \to X$ is affine by Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/01SG" data-tag="01SG">29.11.12</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>